From dc7a2f34f6e866435b51848c3a22418db05775cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 17:20:54 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 01/17] server: Adds support for xdg-activation-v1 protocol.

Creates the wlr_xdg_activation_v1 global and handles `request_activate`
by raising and activating the requested XDG toplevel, if it is mapped on
the current workspace. Any valid token is accepted, so there is no focus
stealing prevention yet.

This is what GTK4 and Qt use to raise an already-running application,
and what launchers use to hand over focus to a newly started client.

Signed-off-by: ruscher <rruscher@gmail.com>
